.TH SYS_PROC_EXE 2 "2026-03-05" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_exe \- query process executable path
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_exe(pid_t " pid ", char *" buf ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_exe ()
copies the path of the program process
.I pid
last executed into
.IR buf ,
at most
.I len
bytes including the terminating NUL.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negated errno is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I buf
is NULL or points outside the caller's address space, or
.I len
is zero.
.TP
.B EPERM
The caller is not root, and the process is not its own: its real or
effective user id differs from the caller's effective one, or it has
changed credentials (set-id exec).
.TP
.B ERANGE
.I len
is too small for the path and its NUL.
.TP
.B ESRCH
.I pid
does not refer to an existing process.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR execve (2),
.BR sys_proc_cwd (2),
.BR sys_proc_info (2)
